  "adaptation": {
    "semantic": "\"course\": the lesson sense, the meal sense, and the direction sense are different words in many languages; check which one is meant.",
    "grammar": null,
    "culture": null,
    "false_friends": "\"course\": a similar-looking word in some languages means one lesson or a race. In English, **a course** is a whole series of lessons; one meeting is **a class** or **a lesson**.",
    "pronunciation": "\"course\" and \"coarse\" sound the same; only the spelling shows which one is meant."
  },
